{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum","id":1160856,"title":"Two Questions About the Spirit Arcanum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-20T08:19:57-08:00","id":1160856,"title":"Two Questions About the Spirit Arcanum","content":"Two (hopefully quick!) requests for clarification on MtAw 2nd Edition Spirit rules:<br /> <br /> <b>1) Can the Spirit Arcanum directly affect Resonance Keywords?</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Resonance&quot; doesn't appear in the list of purviews for the Spirit Arcanum [p.179], and the only listed Spirit spells relating to Resonance target Manifestation Conditions <i>in spite</i> of Resonance, rather than affecting Resonance Keywords directly [see, e.g., &quot;Opener of the Way&quot; and &quot;Erode Resonance&quot;, p. 181]. Resonance <i>is</i> explicitly within the purview of Prime [p. 165], but the only Prime spells that influence Resonance Keywords are restricted to Nodes and Hallows [see, e.g., &quot;Geomancy&quot;, p. 169]. This suggests to me that Prime's purview deals with magically-sourced Resonance only, and not the broader definition of Resonance that governs the Influences of ephemeral entities.<br /> <br /> Muddying the waters further is the write-up for the Resonant Condition [p. 259], which states that &quot;the Spirit and Mind Arcana can instill this Condition by manipulating Resonance, emotions, and thoughts.&quot; Given that the Resonant Condition means nothing more than &quot;the subject of this Condition is within the sphere of Influence of a spirit or Goetia&quot;, this implies that Spirit magic <i>can</i> directly influence Resonance Keywords (with Mind manipulating the &quot;emotions and thoughts&quot; part). And the lack of mention of Prime is further evidence that the Resonance in Prime's purview is treated somehow differently than the Resonance on which the Resonant Manifestation Condition depends.<br /> <br /> So, would it be possible for a Spirit mage to directly impose a &quot;Life&quot; Resonance Keyword on a person/place/thing, thereby attracting spirits of that type and benefiting from the impact of their Influences?<br /> <br /> <b>2) What is the range of the Spirit 3 spell &quot;Spirit Summons&quot;?</b><br /> <br /> I find the wording of the spell to be confusing: &quot;The mage sends out a call to the nearest spirit within her sensory range. Conversely she can summon spirits she knows personally. She may send a general call and the nearest spirit will answer, or she can specify the type of spirit by Resonance.&quot; [p. 182].<br /> <br /> First, it clearly dictates &quot;sensory range&quot; as the range of the spell. <i>But </i>the next sentence begins with &quot;conversely&quot;, suggesting to me that it describes an alternative to the first sentence, rather than a continuation. Then the third sentence repeats the idea of &quot;nearest spirit&quot;, but <i>again</i> seems to offer an alternative (i.e. specifying a type of spirit by Resonance).<br /> <br /> So, is &quot;sensory range&quot; the range in all cases, or are there exceptions for personal knowledge or specifying Resonance?<br /> <br /> If it's always sensory range, then doesn't this make Spirit Summons rather limiting? After all, if the spirit is <i>already </i>in sensory range... why do I have to summon it? Can't I just cast Command Spirit on it right away---a lower-level spell that, in addition to letting me summon the spirit (with a command), also lets me give it a bunch of additional commands of greater complexity than those permitted by spending Reach on Spirit Summons?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for your help!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T08:45:26-08:00","id":1160867,"title":"","content":"What a mess.<br /> <br /> I think you are correct that Prime should affect Supernal resonance and Spirit should affect Spirit-themed resonance.<br /> <br /> As far as the range of Spirit Summons: I think it should be Sensory range regardless of what you are summoning. You either use it to summon:<br /> <br /> a) The nearest spirit<br /> b) The nearest spirit with &quot;X&quot; Resonance<br /> c) A spirit you know<br /> <br /> Sensory range is fairly far and it's possible to extend the range with Space.<br /> <br /> I think the limitation encourages Shamans to have knowledge of their local Spirit ecology to be effective. It keeps Spirit from being a catch-all tool that just lets you summon whatever you want wherever you want. It's still super powerful, but requires more care and study.<br /> <br /> I generally allow Spirit mages to make a case for why a particular spirit should be in the area and as long as they make a decent case I usually allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-20-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T08:54:08-08:00","id":1160876,"title":"","content":"There is no difference between Prime and Spirit Resonance. Prime manipulates Resonance directly, but other arcana manipulate it via reverse engineering. Spirit for instance can slap a spirit into an area where it wouldn\u2019t normally be able to comfortably exist, it can then exert its Influences to make the environment more amenable to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T09:33:10-08:00","id":1160888,"title":"","content":"As for Spirit Summoms it wraps several effects into one spell, including Opener of the Way, Command Spirit, and Reaching. Essentially, it\u2019s a good spell for conserving spell control skits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T10:04:11-08:00","id":1160894,"title":"","content":"At the cost of a fair amount of Reach though.<br /> <br /> How rare would you say that Spirits on this side of the Gauntlet are?<br /> <br /> For instance, in my game a gang used a particular spot of their HQ to torture people who weren't paying their loans. I had a Pain Gaffling attracted to the torture chair that had crossed over due to the amount of Pain resonance. Should I have left that gaffling on the other side of the Gauntlet or do you think it might have been able to cross over.<br /> <br /> So far the Thyrsus in my group is concentrating mostly on Life and only has Spirit 2, but I'd like to handle this stuff better than in my last game and try to have a little more consistency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-20-2017, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T10:15:21-08:00","id":1160898,"title":"","content":"Less Reach than if you were attempting to cast and maintain all those spells at low Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T12:24:25-08:00","id":1160935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1160894#post1160894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, in my game a gang used a particular spot of their HQ to torture people who weren't paying their loans. I had a Pain Gaffling attracted to the torture chair that had crossed over due to the amount of Pain resonance. Should I have left that gaffling on the other side of the Gauntlet or do you think it might have been able to cross over.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should probably have stayed on the other side, unless other factors play into it. Spirits are perfectly capable of feeding from resonance from the shadow, escaping into the real world gives them more agency to create suitable resonances (and respite from being hunten by other spirits), so a spirit who has allready found a stable ecological nieche is less likely to feel pressured to cross over. Generally I treat Shadows crossing over as reasonably rare, as doing so poses a significant risk (namely essence bleed and upset werewolves) which can ultimately lead to its destruction. Main motivations for crossing over are unsated hunger, dangerous pursuit and other stranger occurences.<br /> <br /> tl;dr<br /> <br /> It makes sense to me if the Gaffling is infringing upon that delicious pain resonance from the real world because there's a jaggling there hugging the spot in the shadow that would eat it if it tried to infringe upon its territory otherwise.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T13:37:36-08:00","id":1160957,"title":"","content":"I like that explanation. Thanks. I've already had it played out on this side of The Gauntlet so I'm thankful for an explanation as to why it might have been on this side.<br /> <br /> I take it the 2-dot Spirit attainment doesn't see across the Gauntlet correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-20-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T13:57:00-08:00","id":1160961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1160957#post1160957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take it the 2-dot Spirit attainment doesn't see across the Gauntlet correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, only into Spirit-attuned twilight. However, a Spirit unveiling spell to gaze across the gauntlet into The Shadow isn't too much of a hurdle unless the gauntlet is exceptionally thick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T14:00:15-08:00","id":1160962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1160961#post1160961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, only into Spirit-attuned twilight. However, a Spirit unveiling spell to gaze across the gauntlet into The Shadow isn't too much of a hurdle unless the gauntlet is exceptionally thick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exorcist\u2019s Eye for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T15:19:24-08:00","id":1160984,"title":"","content":"Ok. So Spirit mages aren't constantly walking around seeing Spirits everywhere then really? Just the odd one here and there that crossed over?<br /> <br /> Unless they are specifically peering across the Gauntlet, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T15:22:12-08:00","id":1160985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1160984#post1160984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. So Spirit mages aren't constantly walking around seeing Spirits everywhere then really? Just the odd one here and there that crossed over?<br /> <br /> Unless they are specifically peering across the Gauntlet, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T18:49:19-08:00","id":1161036,"title":"","content":"Another question: How would a gaffling have crossed over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T19:17:31-08:00","id":1161045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1161036#post1161036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question: How would a gaffling have crossed over?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gafflings are pretty weak, Rank 1-2. Barring all the various ways another being could have brought them over, like Shadow Gate or verges, a spirit uses Gauntlet Breach to get across. The roll is penalized by the Gauntlet rating in that area (or granted a bonus, in the case of loci), and requires a Resonant Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-20-2017, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T06:49:07-08:00","id":1161154,"title":"","content":"The Gauntlet may have weakened to almost nothing during the torturing (say, if it happened during a full moon and the victim died there). This might have attracted the Gaffling. It was attacked by another spirit and crossed over to escape. Its been &quot;stuck&quot; ever since. The gauntlet has strengthend and there's still another spirit waiting on the shadow side. <br /> But it gets Essence and is fairly safe. It may even use its violence influence to edge the gang on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T11:54:15-08:00","id":1161231,"title":"","content":"Ok. I like it. Thanks everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T07:48:03-08:00","id":1161517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1160876#post1160876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no difference between Prime and Spirit Resonance. Prime manipulates Resonance directly, but other arcana manipulate it via reverse engineering. Spirit for instance can slap a spirit into an area where it wouldn\u2019t normally be able to comfortably exist, it can then exert its Influences to make the environment more amenable to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that &quot;Resonance&quot;, as a concept, means the same thing whether it's being created by a convergence of ley lines at a Node or by the simple nature of an area, but that doesn't necessarily mean that the Arcana aren't able to distinguish between &quot;Resonance as a result of Nodes, Hallows, ley lines and other sources of Mana&quot; and more general sources of Resonance.<br /> <br /> In fact, there's a lot of evidence to suggest that the opposite is true:<ul><li>The Resonant Manifestation Condition explicitly mentions Spirit as being able to &quot;manipulate Resonance&quot;, but does not mention Prime. Your suggestion that Spirit only does this as a side-effect of summoning spirits is akin to saying that Life can manipulate Resonance by growing a bunch of trees in an area. While this is true, the specific mention of Spirit being able to manipulate Resonance seems to suggest a more direct connection.</li> <li>The only Prime spells that influence Resonance are explicitly restricted to the manipulation of Nodes, Hallows and ley lines: in other words, Resonance as it relates to <i>Mana</i>.</li> <li>Spirit Mage Sight explicitly reveals Resonance (&quot;the nature of the Resonance Condition&quot;), whereas Prime Mage Sight does not mention Resonance at all.</li> <li>Of all of the spells that influence Resonance Keywords, the most versatile is the Spirit 5 spell Essence Fountain [p.185], which permits generating Essence out of nothing with any Resonance Keyword, including multiple Resonance Keywords. Prime spells of the same level are more limited (see, e.g. Create Truth [p. 170], which generates a Hallow with Resonance &quot;appropriate to the location and to the caster's Path and Nimbus&quot;). Comparing the two spells suggests that it's the Spirit mage who has greater command over Resonance.</li> <li>On p. 242: &quot;Prime spells manipulate ley lines by moving them, creating them, or altering their Resonance. Certain Spirit spells manipulate Resonance as well.&quot; (Again restricting Prime's manipulation of Resonance to sources of Mana, with a less specific nod towards Spirit's ability to manipulate Resonance in general.)</li> </ul><br /> So, in short... I remain confused. The rules on which Arcana, if any, can directly influence the Resonance Keywords of a person, place or thing seem to all agree that &quot;general&quot; Resonance is a Spirit Arcanum thing, except for the fact that there aren't any listed Spirit spells that actually do this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1160888#post1160888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Spirit Summoms it wraps several effects into one spell, including Opener of the Way, Command Spirit, and Reaching. Essentially, it\u2019s a good spell for conserving spell control skits.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems... weak to me. A whole dot more for a <i>weaker </i>version of Command Spirit whose only advantage is to combine other spells of arguable value, and only then by spending Reach? It doesn't even permit a spirit to cross the Gauntlet, and with the extra commands you get from Spirit 2's Command Spirit, it's hardly difficult to simply command the spirit to use its Influence to create the Open Condition on its own (after all, if the spirit is in sensory range, then it's probably already in an area with the appropriate Resonant Condition).<br /> <br /> On one hand, I kind of like the idea of a Spirit Summons spell that requires you to go hunting for spirits in areas that are likely to attract them... but at the table, this requires a lot of one-on-one time between spirit mage and Storyteller. And how does a spirit mage take advantage of the court they've cultivated during play, without the ability to summon them from afar? Do we assume friendly spirits remain in sensory range of the mage at all times, like Twilight groupies?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T08:09:51-08:00","id":1161521,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t have time to address everything at the moment, but Spirit Simmons does let you breach the Gauntlet to bring a spirit through for a Reach. Also, of course Command Spirit is better at actually being able to compel a spirit, it isn\u2019t doing nearly as much work as Spirit Summons.<br /> <br /> \u201cFriendly\u201d (Spirits are naturally antagonistic to Mages as a general rule) spirits can be Fettered to appropriate objects, and bound as Familiars, there\u2019s no reason a Thyrsus would go anywhere without some spirits. Space 2 can allow you to extend Spirit Summons to Sympathetic range if you have some spirits you usually leave at home.<br /> <br /> Also, there\u2019s nothing wrong with a character having some solo spotlight time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T09:52:10-08:00","id":1161540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1161521#post1161521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t have time to address everything at the moment, but Spirit Simmons does let you breach the Gauntlet to bring a spirit through for a Reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't. It lets you summon a spirit from the opposite side of the Gauntlet, but it doesn't let you bring the spirit through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1161521#post1161521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, of course Command Spirit is better at actually being able to compel a spirit, it isn\u2019t doing nearly as much work as Spirit Summons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point I'm making is that, if Spirit Summons is limited to targets in &quot;sensory range&quot;, then it seems to be almost entirely trumped by Command Spirit---which can target sensory range for a Reach, like any other spell, and allows you to issue multiple, complex commands to the target spirit. If one of those is &quot;come to me&quot;, then you've &quot;summoned&quot; the spirit with a spell a full dot lower, <i>and</i> you have a bunch more complex commands to give it on top of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1161521#post1161521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cFriendly\u201d (Spirits are naturally antagonistic to Mages as a general rule) spirits can be Fettered to appropriate objects, and bound as Familiars, there\u2019s no reason a Thyrsus would go anywhere without some spirits. Space 2 can allow you to extend Spirit Summons to Sympathetic range if you have some spirits you usually leave at home.</div> </div> </div> </div>There may be no reason a Thyrsus with Spirit 4 won't go anywhere without spirits, or a mage with command of both Spirit and Space, but that's a heavy investment for the basic functionality of having access to the occasional spirit to aid you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1161521#post1161521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there\u2019s nothing wrong with a character having some solo spotlight time.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, of course you're right, but it's a question of degree: &quot;some&quot; vs. &quot;a lot&quot;, to be specific.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T09:57:54-08:00","id":1161541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1161521#post1161521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Spirits are naturally antagonistic to Mages as a general rule)</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh what? I mean spirits can be pretty antagonistic (after a sort) in general, but why would they be naturally antagonistic towards mages in general? Or do you just mean &quot;they'd be antagonistic towards mages as they would be towards any human&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T09:59:48-08:00","id":1161542,"title":"","content":"I think Spirit Summons is pretty good. Your first command can be &quot;Stand before me and be still&quot;. Then you can drop the Summons and cast Command Spirit for further commands.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Prime/Spirit Resonance situation needs to be cleared up. It's a mess right now.<br /> <br /> The Spirit Summons range issue might be one of those things where the fact that range is determined by Sympathy and Sympathy is very personal makes it a hard thing for standard Thyrsus Arcana to duplicate a standard trope like summoning some spirit from 1000 miles away to just appear in your summoning circle.<br /> <br /> I mean, with Spirit 2 and Space 3 and a Sympathetic connection to the Spirit you could just open a portal and command a spirit to come to you from where it is, but default Thyrsus that don't invest in Space aren't really going to be able to do that.<br /> <br /> Sounds like a Space-based Spirit Summoning Legacy is in order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-22-2017, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T10:08:57-08:00","id":1161545,"title":"","content":"Reread the Reach clause, you\u2019re right it can\u2019t bring the spirit across. I was thrown off by it mentioning that it contends with Gauntlet strength. Not sure what to say about that. <br /> <br /> Leaving that out, Spirit Simmons can accomplish at least one thing that Command Spirit can\u2019t which is to place the Open Condition on the area even if it would normally be inhospitable to the spirit, save a spell control slot. It\u2019s also Duration primary instead of Potency as Command Spirit is. YMMV on that. Spirit Summoms also negates a spirit\u2019s ability to fight a command to act against its own interest with a CoW.<br /> <br /> You only need Spirit 2 to create conditions on an object or your person that make it a place a spirit can reside, or to invest Merit dots to get a familiar. Space 2 isn\u2019t that big an investment imo, you can start with it.<br /> <br /> As for the degree, that concern is table specific and it\u2019s up to the ST to pace things properly so that no one is being left out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T10:10:46-08:00","id":1161547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1161542#post1161542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a Space-based Spirit Summoning Legacy is in order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Made one of those once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T23:02:41-08:00","id":1161767,"title":"","content":"So regarding resonance and Prime/Spirit. Seeing as one of the explicit purviews of prime is resonance, is there any particular reason it should be limited on the resonance it can affect? Now you'd need to be able to see essence to effect it, Yes, but aside from that hurdle? It seems like a prime 3 weaving spell should be more than capable of temporarily altering resonance conditions and even the resonant nature of certain things. As an aside, some of the Prime 5 spells feel woefully inadequate for their level. Blasphemy is just depressing, and I wish it worked kinda like Ansho, and although the flavor of create truth is nice, should it really be restricted as it is? I mean, a creative thaumaturgy spell at that level certainly feels like it'd be able to accomplish wholesale and relatively unfettered creation.<br /> <br /> Anyway, minor rant on Prime 5 aside, I think given the particular purview of prime one should allow it to affect all resonance conditions, probably. I mean, It's not &quot;magical-resonance&quot; or &quot;supernal-resonance&quot; but rather a seperate explicit entity just as truth is all truth, not just supernal truth, despite Prime being quite heavily focused on magic and mana. He'll, mana's even listed separately, so maybe that's an even stronger case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","user":"PixelPuzzler","date":". 11-23-2017, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12093-pixelpuzzler","name":"PixelPuzzler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T03:06:55-08:00","id":1161805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PixelPuzzler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1161767#post1161767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So regarding resonance and Prime/Spirit. Seeing as one of the explicit purviews of prime is resonance, is there any particular reason it should be limited on the resonance it can affect?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that this is only one relevant section in the rules, and it's contradicted in various other places in the book (I've listed them all in bullet points a few posts up). One of the most telling, in my opinion, is in the write-ups for Mage Sight: Prime does not reveal Resonance, while Spirit explicitly does. There's also the fact that the Spirit 5 Essence-creation spell gives much more flexibility in choosing multiple Resonance Keywords, while the equivalent Prime 5 spell for creating Hallows specifically <i>prohibits </i>the mage from choosing the Resonance at all (it's determined by the mage's nimbus and path).<br /> <br /> Likewise, literally <i>all </i>references to, or examples of, Prime affecting Resonance are explicitly restricted to Nodes, Hallows and ley lines---there is literally no mention, nor even a hint, that Prime can affect Resonance outside of that restriction. On the other hand, there are numerous examples of Spirit being said to affect Resonance without any such limitations, sometimes in the same sentence as a more-restricted mention of Prime (e.g. &quot;Prime spells manipulate ley lines by moving them, creating them, or altering their Resonance. Certain Spirit spells manipulate Resonance as well.&quot;) The Resonant Condition, which is really just a placeholder for &quot;matching Resonance Keyword&quot;, lists Spirit and Mind as the only two Arcana that can affect Resonance (presumably, Mind does so for Goetia, while Spirit does so for spirits).<br /> <br /> In short, the rules are contradictory and completely unclear on this subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T06:08:56-08:00","id":1162708,"title":"","content":"Probably has to do with how the two Arcana have different perspectives on Resonance.<br /> <br /> To Prime, Resonance is Supernal energy seeping out through the cracks of Fallen reality. So to Prime, Resonance looks like rivers and geographical faults, and that's pretty much what ley lines and nodes are. So Prime gets to have &quot;Resonance&quot; as its explicit purview, for all things Supernal are of Prime, but actual Prime spells that manipulate Resonance do so in a context that fits in with how the Supernal World interacts with Resonance - as ley lines and nodes.<br /> <br /> To Spirit, Resonance is still Supernal bleed-over, but more importantly it's also the life-stuff of spirits and the breath of the Shadow. So to Spirit, Resonance is not an environmental feature, but the environment itself. So Spirit doesn't get &quot;Resonance&quot; as its explicit purview, but it still gets to affect Resonance for the same reason you need to control the fuel to control the fire. Thus Spirit spells that manipulate Resonance do so in a context that fits in with how the Shadow interacts with Resonance - as Manifestation Conditions and Essence.<br /> <br /> Or at least, that's the message that I got. Dunno if that's what the writers intended, but it made sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T16:06:47-08:00","id":1162818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1160856-two-questions-about-the-spirit-arcanum?p=1162708#post1162708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably has to do with how the two Arcana have different perspectives on Resonance.<br /> <br /> To Prime, Resonance is Supernal energy seeping out through the cracks of Fallen reality. So to Prime, Resonance looks like rivers and geographical faults, and that's pretty much what ley lines and nodes are. So Prime gets to have &quot;Resonance&quot; as its explicit purview, for all things Supernal are of Prime, but actual Prime spells that manipulate Resonance do so in a context that fits in with how the Supernal World interacts with Resonance - as ley lines and nodes.<br /> <br /> To Spirit, Resonance is still Supernal bleed-over, but more importantly it's also the life-stuff of spirits and the breath of the Shadow. So to Spirit, Resonance is not an environmental feature, but the environment itself. So Spirit doesn't get &quot;Resonance&quot; as its explicit purview, but it still gets to affect Resonance for the same reason you need to control the fuel to control the fire. Thus Spirit spells that manipulate Resonance do so in a context that fits in with how the Shadow interacts with Resonance - as Manifestation Conditions and Essence.<br /> <br /> Or at least, that's the message that I got. Dunno if that's what the writers intended, but it made sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes... absolutely perfect sense to me. Thank you! As far as I'm concerned, this is canon in my games. (The thing I was missing was a reasonable explanation of Spirit's interaction with Resonance being limited to Manifestation Conditions, rather than the ability to affect Keywords directly. Your explanation makes sense to me, and justifies what I'd come to intuitively thing: that no Arcanum can directly influence Resonance Keywords on the environment, without extenuating circumstances.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">Amateur dinosaur hunter and extreme weather enthusiast, whose interests include spoken mime, armchair parkour, conspicuous ninjutsu and Schr\u00f6edinger's pentameter\u2014of which this sentence may or may not be an example.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13110-eunomiac","name":"Eunomiac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}